Description: A single, consistent interface to established models of social
    network processes. Influence models describe how a node characteristic
    changes as a function of its prior state and of network exposure to the
    characteristics of connected others. Selection models describe how network
    ties change as a function of sender, receiver, dyadic, and higher-order
    structural effects. The package provides a canonical data
    structure for node, tie, and group data, a modular exposure engine, a
    formula grammar spanning both model families, design and estimation
    diagnostics, effect sizes, and a visualization layer. It implements,
    integrates, and operationalizes published methods. Its main extension is
    its own construction from published components: a hierarchical multi-group
    Selection model with random intercepts and slopes across groups. This and
    the package's smaller constructions are documented as such. Developed and
    owned by Griffin Dynamics LLC as part of its ongoing research and
    development. The author acknowledges the T.A.C.T.I.C.S Lab at the
    University of South Florida, and thanks Ken Frank for his support and
    insights.
